-Monitoring will consist of measuring flow rates and collecting samples for field analysis (pH, specific conductance, temperature, and turbidity) and laboratory analysis (Table 2). The parameters to be measured and analyzed from the surface water samples are from the NDEP Profile I and/or Profile II lists as shown in Table 2, with metals and common ions to be analyzed as total. Also included in Table 2 are NDEP Reference Values that are used as water quality guideline values. In addition, surface water quality standards are included in NAC 445A.1236 for the following categories: municipal or domestic supply; aquatic life; irrigation; and watering of livestock. Sampling will occur quarterly or semi-annually for one of the downstream Thacker Creek sites, which has continuous flow monitoring. Monitoring of selected springs near the Project area also will occur quarterly or semi­ annually.
+Monitoring will consist of measuring flow rates and collecting samples for analysis, as appropriate. Parameters and frequency will be determined at a later date.
 
